From f792f3075ff3243711febb432aa567a6a0bd098a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:56:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Scope extended Bazel deadlines to their slow test suites

Keep the daemon, core-all, app-server-all and exec-all deadlines while
returning their short sibling suites to the short default. Give binary
unit tests a separate timeout so the TUI library override does not
inflate tiny binary tests. Wine and Windows-cross inherit the selected
native integration override; sharding and assertions remain unchanged.

Base: rust-v0.163.0 (83086188ae0614bd882818ff1aa23f3194962012),
with the current queue through macOS thread-budget source e7acc0261.
TDD: the timeout suite fails five new assertions on the unchanged source
(expected short, got moderate/long), exit 3. With the fix, all 20
analysis tests pass, including long-suite and Wine controls, exit 0.
Command: bash .github/scripts/run-bazel-ci.sh --print-failed-test-logs --
  test --jobs=4 -- //tools/build-warnings/test-timeouts:timeouts_tests
Local invocations use run-local-rust and explicitly owned Bazel storage.
Execution record: timeout-ownership.json in the active CI repair work.
